  "findings": [
    "Fixed TRAIN total loss improves1.832358166→1.823357637, while later total loss is2.360385095→2.360440765. Better TRAIN fit does not establish better later forecasts.",
    "M15 conditional-side Brier/log improves for both S and F in both pointwise day/week intervals. Its AUC change includes zero; this supports a probability/calibration effect rather than established ranking improvement.",
    "M5F AUC changes0.528605973→0.526009515, Brier0.249511328→0.249473211. Both changes remain uncertain in both day/week intervals.",
    "H4S Brier/log deteriorates in both pointwise day/week intervals. H1S log also deteriorates in both; its Brier week interval includes zero. Other point deteriorations must not be called conclusive.",
    "All10 later S/F AUC-delta intervals include zero under both grouping schemes. There is no established overall later directional gain from this change.",
    "Future M15 meanPup falls0.615858→0.594687 against observed0.491060. H1 remains0.624343→0.624724 against0.5; D1 rises0.638159→0.689883 against0.575089. Separate side heads alone did not remove the residual probability bias.",
    "TRAIN future H4/D1 AUC improves0.577979→0.604648 and0.652998→0.684418; later H4/D1 remains0.516436/0.491324. This is a measured training-versus-later gap, not a proof of its representation or market-regime cause.",
    "The mixed result does not justify promoting the combination or another architecture change on its own. The source variant remains available; no genuine indicator/timeframe is removed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only the existing combined decoder is contrasted at matched initialization, exposure and update budget; later shared-weight changes are part of the learned response.",
    "Later panel is reused development; original TRAIN is not untouched holdout.",
    "Conditional-side support uses realized labels and does not establish selectable Entry coverage.",
    "Day/week percentile95 intervals are pointwise exploratory with overlapping targets; no multiplicity-adjusted or regime-wide guarantee.",
    "No model, checkpoint, feature payload, new fitting, TEST, trade-path, PnL or promotion.",
    "A short fixed-budget contrast does not establish full model capacity, the value of all available training years or a30–40epoch outcome.",
    "Shared encoder/query interference, feature sufficiency and stable signal across market regimes are not isolated by this contrast.",
    "Technical baseline/receipt success, TRAIN fit, independent generalization and trading economics remain separate claims."
  ],
